			name: 'create',
			method: 'POST',
			route: 'tasks/create',
			versioned: true,
			summary: 'Task creation',
			description:
				'To access the method, the following permission is required task_write . Method creates the task and returns its internal ID. If it is needed to change the task execution date, it is necessary to transmit date in Y-m-d H:i format to the task[datetime] field. Date should be in the future. In the task[performerId] field it is required to pass the internal ID of the user or group to assign the responsible user/group You can pass the task priority in the task[priority] field. Available values are: low - low priority; medium - medium priority; high - high priority. If the field is not passed, the task will automatically get the medium priority. If it is needed to relate the task with existing customer, then it is necessary to set the value of one of the following fields: task[customer][id] – customer internal ID; task[customer][externalId] – customer external ID. If the values of several fields are set, they will be processed in the ordering specified above. Customer search will be made within stores, which the used API-key has access to. If customer will not be found, relation will not be set. If it is needed to relate task with existing order, then it is necessary to set the value of one of the following fields: task[order][id] – order internal ID; task[order][externalId] – external order ID; task[order][number] – order number. If the values of several fields are set, they will be processed in the ordering specified above. Order search will be made within stores, which the used API-key has access to. If order will not be found, relation will not be set. When relating the task with existing order, task will be automatically related with customer, which the order belongs to. If it is needed to relate task with existing ticket, then it is necessary to set the value of one of the following fields: task[ticket][id] – ticket internal ID; task[ticket][externalId] – external ticket ID; task[ticket][number] – ticket number. If the values of several fields are set, they will be processed in the ordering specified above. Ticket search will be made within stores, which the used API-key has access to. If ticket will not be found, relation will not be set. When passing task[ticket][externalId] or task[ticket][number] , the store symbolic code must also be passed in the site parameter. When relating the task with existing ticket, task will be automatically related with customer, which the ticket belongs to. When binding the task with customer, order, or ticket, it is necessary to specify either customer data or order and/or ticket data. When creating the task for recall you should specify phone number, which has to be called, in the task[phone] field. It is desirable to specify the symbolic code of store in task[phoneSite] field for having opportunity to make recall from the certain store phone. This opportunity depends on used telephony and its settings.',
