			summary: 'get_intaro_crm_api_tickets_list_v5',
			description:
				'To access the method, the following permission is required ticket_read . Tickets are ordered by creation date and ID, descending. For the next page, pass pagination.nextCursor as cursor and keep the same filters. An empty cursor marks the end of the list. Record and SLA changes between requests may affect the results. The sites codes are intersected with the stores accessible to the API key. Inactive reference entries can also be used in filters. Dates use Y-m-d , with both boundary days included in full. Status, type, topic and assignee filters apply to ticket issues. Different conditions may match different issues, but both closing date bounds must match the same issue. All issues are returned. completed includes tickets without issues. Customer filters apply to customer . All specified segments and regular tags must match. For attached tags, one match is enough. Regular and attached tag filters can be combined. vip and bad are applied independently, including false . customFields supports active fields enabled for filtering. Numeric min and max bounds must be integers from 0 to 2147483647 for integer fields and to 100000000000 for numeric fields. As in other REST lists, min=0 does not restrict the lower bound, and max=0 without min selects zero and empty values. Set both bounds to 0 to match zero exactly. For date and datetime fields, specify days in Y-m-d format.',
